# OpenMicroCam: the kernel configuration that matches the module ABI of the YIZHAN 4K camera's stock kernel (SigmaStar
# SSC8836 / Mercury6, Linux 4.9.227), as a minimal config over vanilla 4.9.227 for ARCH=arm. prepare-ktree.sh applies it.
# The lines hold: vermagic «4.9.227 SMP preempt mod_unload ARMv7 thumb2 p2v8» (SMP, PREEMPT, MODULE_UNLOAD,
# THUMB2_KERNEL; no MODVERSIONS, no LOCALVERSION), the layout of struct module (PERF_EVENTS, JUMP_LABEL, ARM_MODULE_PLTS,
# FTRACE off), of struct device and the locks (CMA, DMA_CMA, DEBUG_SPINLOCK, DEBUG_MUTEXES), the L2 cache calls
# (CACHE_L2X0 off) and the USB core and gadget core as modules (USB, USB_GADGET =m); DEBUG_KERNEL is the debug options' gate.
# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS=y
CONFIG_JUMP_LABEL=y
CONFIG_MODULES=y
CONFIG_MODULE_UNLOAD=y
# CONFIG_CACHE_L2X0 is not set
CONFIG_SMP=y
CONFIG_PREEMPT=y
CONFIG_THUMB2_KERNEL=y
CONFIG_ARM_MODULE_PLTS=y
CONFIG_CMA=y
CONFIG_DMA_CMA=y
CONFIG_USB=m
CONFIG_USB_GADGET=m
CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_SPINLOCK=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_MUTEXES=y
# CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
